Materials Processing — MIT 3.044, Spring 2013 (@mat-mit-processing: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mat-sources) { r_5RCMWE5WA6D0WS1ETHWRZVXMFR
Chris Schuh, MIT OpenCourseWare. [Course and lecture notes](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/3-044-materials-processing-spring-2013/pages/lecture-notes/), [syllabus](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/3-044-materials-processing-spring-2013/pages/syllabus/), [assignments](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/3-044-materials-processing-spring-2013/pages/assignments/), [exams](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/3-044-materials-processing-spring-2013/pages/exams/).

Read the complete available sequence and work the public problems before consulting solutions. Heat transfer, flow, casting, polymer/glass shaping, colloids and powder consolidation connect process rate with material quality. Use the shared full thermal/fluid texts for derivations omitted from these compact undergraduate notes. The readings page names commercial textbooks; their contents are not included by this link.

The syllabus/index and selected lecture 20–21 PDFs were inspected on 30 October 2026. Lecture 20 is four pages, internally dated May 2012; lecture 21 is seven pages. Lecture 12 has no posted notes and lecture 17 was canceled. MIT OCW states CC BY-NC-SA with component exceptions. Keep credits and source files external.

